I have an AlphaPC 164LX box, which did not have a graphics card.  I've
added a PCI ATI Radeon 7000, which googling suggested should work fine
in this machine, but I have not had any success in getting it to work.

The SRM is quite happy with the new card; I compiled a new 2.4.18 kernel
with the radeon DRI code (I tried the framebuffer too, but that kernel
panics as soon as it boots).

I obtained the most recent XFree86 4.2.0 packages I could find, on
Branden's site.

Attempting to start X fails with a fairly nasty graphics subsystem
lockup which requires a reboot to fix.

scanpci finds the card:

pci bus 0x0000 cardnum 0x09 function 0x00: vendor 0x1002 device 0x5159
 ATI Radeon VE QY

and the appropriate device section of my XF86Config-4 is:

Section "Device"
        Identifier      "Radeon"
        Driver  "radeon"
        BusID   "PCI:00:09:00"
        Screen  0
EndSection

The log file seems to suggest that the int10 module is the culprit - but
I have int10 commented out in the XF86Config-4 file, so I don't know
where that's come from:

